# JPool TypeScript SDK — Development Guide

## Project Overview
Solana liquid staking SDK (`@jpool/sdk`). Pool address: `CtMyWsrUtAwXWiGr9WjHT5fC3p3fgV8cyGpLTo2LJzG1`

## Required Context
Always read these files when starting any task to ensure correct context:
- `package.json` — dependencies, scripts
- `src/constants.ts` — pool addresses, API URLs
- `src/types.ts` — TypeScript interfaces
- `tsconfig.json` — compiler options
- `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production` — RPC endpoints and keys (if present)
- `~/.config/solana/id.json` — local Solana keypair (needed for example scripts)

## Code Standards
- TypeScript strict mode (`"strict": true`)
- ESM + CJS dual output via tsup
- Use `@solana/web3.js` v1.x patterns (PublicKey, Connection, Transaction)
- All public methods must have JSDoc with `@param` and `@returns`
- Prefer `bigint` over `BN.js` for numeric values
- Error handling: throw typed errors, never return null for failures

## Testing
- Run examples: `npx tsx example/info.ts`
- Build check: `pnpm build`
- Lint: `pnpm lint`

## Solana-Specific Rules
- Always validate PublicKey inputs with `try { new PublicKey(input) }`
- Use `Connection.getLatestBlockhash()` not deprecated `getRecentBlockhash()`
- Memo instructions: use `@solana/spl-memo` for ref/direct-stake memos
- Transaction size limit: max 1232 bytes
